Open the next window asked for as a column at an index

OpenNextWindowOn (opens-next-window-on.patch) puts a window on the
workspace asked for, wherever niri adds it there, and niri moves only
the focused column to an index, so the shell putting a reopened session
back in its column took the focus to do it: Reopen Them All moved
Joel's focus once for every session it reopened.

OpenNextWindowOn gains `column`, the index from 1 the window opens at
as a new column, the last past the last, as niri's own
NewColumnAt places it, so it opens where it goes without the focus
moving. Without it, the window is added as before.

